# Accepted dependency vulnerabilities.
#
# Every line is CVE-ID, then a comment saying why it is accepted and when that
# decision expires. An entry with no expiry is a permanent exception and needs
# a reason that will still be true next year.
#
# Trivy already skips findings with no released fix (`ignore-unfixed: true` in
# .github/workflows/ci.yml), so anything that reaches this file is something we
# could upgrade away from and have chosen not to. That should be rare.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-2000-0000 exp:2026-12-31   # why, and who decided
